+INDEPENDENT OPERATIONAL-BRIDGE REVIEW
+
+Frozen sources compared:
+- verification.k lines 10-267 (definitions and seven domain lemmas)
+- reference-semantics/semantics/core.k lines 217-229 (ValSeq/IntSeq constructors and lengths)
+- reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k lines 7-18 (valSeqAt/intSeqAt)
+- reference-semantics/semantics/list.k lines 18-24 and 52-55 (concatenation and append)
+- reference-semantics/semantics/int.k lines 10-24 (integer arithmetic, comparison, pyMod)
+- solution.py (row-major scan, neighbor minimum, repeated [1, neighbor], optional odd 1)
+- each target parameter's recorded kore_symbol and source_rule_ids
+
+Candidate declaration (Proof.lean) | Independent meaning comparison | Judgment
+
+_andBool_ (199) | Bool && is K andBool on SortBool=Bool. | exact
+«_>=Int_» (201) | decide (a >= b) is K integer >= returning Bool. | exact
+«_<Int_» (203) | decide (a < b) is K integer < returning Bool. | exact
+«_==Int_» (205) | decide (a = b) is K integer equality returning Bool. | exact
+«_+Int_» (207) | Lean Int addition is K +Int on mathematical integers. | exact
+«_*Int_» (209) | Lean Int multiplication is K *Int on mathematical integers. | exact
+gridAt (211; model 22-26) | p[i*n+j], with pAtTotal's 0 default for negative/OOB indices. | exact
+gridRow (213; model 28-30) | constructs j=0..n-1 row-major integer values; n.toNat gives empty for n<=0 exactly as guarded gridRowFrom. | exact
+gridRows (215; model 32-36) | constructs i=0..n-1 list-wrapped rows; n.toNat gives empty for n<=0 exactly as gridRowsFrom. | exact
+oddDone (217; model 48-64) | appends r.toNat [1,m] pairs, then tests O = prefix++[1]; r<=0 maps to zero steps. This is the K base/recurrence. | exact
+oneCol (219; model 66,76-81) | first index of 1 modulo positive n using normalized tmod; returns 0 when n<=0. This matches findOne/oneIndex/pyMod/oneCol. | exact
+oneRow (221; model 69-74) | first index of 1 divided by positive n; returns 0 when n<=0. On valid permutations the index is nonnegative, so Nat quotient equals K /Int. Absent-1 case uses tdiv(-1,n), matching the frozen total definition. | exact
+pairDone (223; model 48-58) | appends r.toNat [1,m] pairs and compares with O; r<=0 maps to the K base case. | exact
+snocVS (225; model 45-46) | constructor-preserving list conversion followed by ++[x], exactly the snocVS base/step recurrence. | exact
+valSeqAt (227-228; model 38-40) | ordinary constructor indexing agrees with the imported valSeqAt equations at every defined nonnegative in-bounds point used by all obligations/source executions. The imported [total] function intentionally leaves OOB/opaque cases abstract; choosing noneV there is a conservative total realization and cannot affect any guarded obligation. | exact on all operationally specified and reachable cases; acceptable total realization elsewhere
+valSeqConcat (230-231; model 42-43) | constructor-preserving list append is exactly the imported base/step valSeqConcat definition and list.append heap update. | exact
+validPerm (233; model 83-87) | 0<=m and Perm [1..m] is equivalent to length=m, every value in [1,m], and uniqueness. For m<0 both definitions are false. | exact
+vsLen (235; model 89-90) | constructor count as Int is exactly the imported .ValSeq/vCons length recurrence. | exact
+
+The bridge is not inferred from the successful proof. It was checked against the frozen equations and program. Actual Lean examples covered ordinary and adversarial values (negative grid index, invalid duplicate permutation, negative permutation size), while independent finite tests covered all seven lemmas over 46,648 cases. Two compiled counterfactuals independently replaced gridAt by constant zero and snocVS by identity; Proof.final then failed at the expected obligations. A separate model audit also identified that constant-false validPerm or constant-equal oddDone/pairDone could vacuously satisfy parts of targetStatement, which is why those actual candidate definitions were inspected rather than accepted from the theorem alone.
+
